&lt;p&gt;SingleStore is looking for an accomplished sales professional to join our Sales Team. AI is moving from experimentation into production, and this role is an opportunity to break into AI while doing meaningful enterprise selling.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As an Account Executive, AI Hunter, your job is simple: create new SingleStore customers. You will find companies building AI applications where data access, real-time context, memory, retrieval, or operational scale is becoming a constraint—and turn those challenges into new SingleStore customers. You will own a broad territory, build a majority self-sourced pipeline, create demand in an emerging category, and close greenfield enterprise opportunities.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a true hunting role. You will engage customers before they have a defined project, develop customer-specific points of view, create urgency around business and technical problems, work with technical experts to land first production workloads, and build a measurable new-logo business with broad ownership. The ideal candidate is a measurable enterprise hunter who is competitive, curious, technically credible, resilient, and able to sell business outcomes. Direct AI sales experience is valuable, but proven selling ability and technical curiosity matter more than a narrow “AI seller” title.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Role and Responsibilities&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and execute a territory strategy for net-new customer acquisition.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prospect fearlessly across a broad account universe using proactive, persistent outbound, account-based, partner, and market-education motions; stay resilient and effective through rejection and ambiguity.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Form account hypotheses, map the buying center, and earn first meetings with relevant points of view tailored to the customer.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Engage executive, business, technical, security, and procurement stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead great business-first discovery, connect AI and data challenges to fundable goals, and build quantified ROI, TCO, or operational-impact cases.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and develop champions, multi-thread the buying group, earn executive and economic-buyer access, and maintain stakeholder alignment; own the stakeholder plan, mutual action plan, close plan, value case, stage gates, forecast, and commercial outcome.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead complex sales cycles through technical validation, security, legal, procurement, negotiation, and close.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Solutions and Forward Deployment Engineers and cross-functional teams to validate technical fit and establish the first production workload.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Navigate competitive displacement and maintain disciplined activity management, CRM hygiene, reporting, qualification, forecasting, and opportunity management; showcase clear metrics such as pipeline created, meetings, conversion, quota attainment, and new-logo performance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Be AI fluent: use AI and research tools productively and responsibly while applying judgment, validating outputs, and separating facts from hypotheses.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Travel within the assigned territory as required.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Required Skills and Experience&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of quota-carrying B2B enterprise software sales experience, ideally selling to large or technically sophisticated organizations; experience in data, cloud, analytics, AI, or adjacent technical domains is a plus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Repeated, quantified quota success with clear ownership of new-logo wins and self-sourced pipeline.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience closing complex, multi-stakeholder deals involving executives, technical evaluators, security, legal, finance, procurement, and partners.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to sell measurable business outcomes and build ROI, TCO, or operational-impact cases.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Technical fluency in an adjacent domain such as databases, data infrastructure, analytics, AI/ML, cloud, Kubernetes, developer tools, cybersecurity, observability, or open-source software.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong qualification, account planning, forecasting, CRM, negotiation, and deal-management skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Learning velocity and coachability, demonstrated through specific behavior change after feedback; ability to explain technical concepts clearly to technical and executive audiences.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Executive presence, customer trust, resilience, intellectual honesty, and excellent communication skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;B.A., B.S. degree or equivalent in a related field.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with Fortune 500 or security-sensitive organizations, cloud ecosystems, open-source or consumption-based products, or emerging categories is preferred.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Fluent in French and/or German&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.fr/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in France</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;GitLab is the intelligent orchestration platform for DevSecOps. GitLab enables organizations to increase developer productivity, improve operational efficiency, reduce security and compliance risk, and accelerate digital transformation. More than 50 million registered users and more than 50% of the Fortune 100* trust GitLab to ship better, more secure software faster.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The same principles built into our products are reflected in how our team works: we embrace AI as a core productivity multiplier, with all team members expected to incorporate AI into their daily workflows to drive efficiency, innovation, and impact. GitLab is where careers accelerate, innovation flourishes, and every voice is valued. Our high-performance culture is driven by our values&amp;nbsp;and continuous knowledge exchange, enabling our team members to reach their full potential while collaborating with industry leaders to solve complex problems. &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=OuZIb5zszQI&quot;&gt;Co-create the future with us&lt;/a&gt; as we build technology that transforms how the world develops software.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;*&lt;em&gt;Fortune 500® is a registered trademark of Fortune Media IP Limited, used under license. Claim based on GitLab data. Fortune 100 refers to the top 20% ranked companies in the 2025 Fortune 500 list, published in June 2025. Fortune and Fortune Media IP Limited are not affiliated with, and do not endorse products or services of GitLab.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;An overview of this role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Professional Services Technical Architect at GitLab, you&#39;ll lead the technical direction of customer engagements from early scoping and discovery through delivery. You&#39;ll design high-level architectures and implementation plans for GitLab infrastructure and functionality, and you&#39;ll make sure deliverables align with customer requirements and the Statement of Work (SOW). You&#39;ll coordinate and guide implementation work across GitLab Professional Services and partner consultants, support customers deploying GitLab in cloud and on-premises environments using tools like Terraform, Ansible, and the GitLab Environment Toolkit, and perform migrations to GitLab using Congregate. You&#39;ll provide DevOps and DevSecOps consulting and best practices, contribute reusable collateral such as documentation, delivery kits, and training materials, and share product release updates to help the team deliver consistent outcomes. This role combines deep technical expertise with customer-facing leadership in GitLab&#39;s remote, asynchronous, and values-driven environment.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Designing and delivering GitLab reference architecture implementations for both self-managed and cloud environments, using infrastructure as code practices&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Leading source code management and CI/CD migrations to GitLab, including large-scale enterprise moves using Congregate&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Building repeatable delivery kits, documentation, and enablement materials that help Professional Services and partners deploy and adopt GitLab best practices&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead the full technical delivery lifecycle for GitLab Professional Services engagements, from early scoping and technical discovery through implementation and handoff.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Produce high-level and detailed technical designs for GitLab infrastructure and functionality, ensuring deliverables align with customer requirements and expectations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Evaluate and communicate scalability and security considerations (including compliance constraints) in proposed GitLab reference architectures and implementation plans.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deploy and configure GitLab in customer environments, including on-premises and major cloud providers, using Terraform, Ansible, and the GitLab Environment Toolkit (GET) aligned to reference architectures.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Plan and execute source system migrations to GitLab using Congregate, partnering closely with customer stakeholders to reduce risk, protect data integrity, and minimize downtime.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide DevOps and DevSecOps consulting and best-practice guidance, including advising on internal frameworks such as the Delivery Governance Framework (DGF) and GitLab Flow.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate and oversee implementation work across GitLab team members, partners, and customer points of contact (POCs), ensuring clear asynchronous communication and decision capture, effective execution, and high-quality outcomes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mentor Professional Services and partner consultants by contributing documentation, delivery kits, and training materials, and by leading enablement sessions on how to deliver and position service offerings.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain and improve delivery automation assets with an emphasis on code cleanliness, maintainability, and appropriate unit/integration testing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support scoping and Statement of Work (SOW) creation with Professional Services Engagement Managers, stay current on monthly GitLab releases, and help Regional Delivery Managers with technical vetting and staffing assessments while maintaining a 55% billable utilization.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Review and provide input to Professional Services training materials and presentations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop case studies, presentations, design documentation, and best-practice methodologies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work closely with customer project teams to ensure accurate task-level articulation of work required&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll bring&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong written and verbal communication skills, including the ability to lead technical discussions with customers and partners and communicate risks/trade-offs clearly in an asynchronous environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Prefer location in PST, MST or CST timezone alignment.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Comfortable with up to 30% travel at times.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Demonstrated experience delivering two or more of the following consulting services: source code management migration, cloud architecture, DevOps engineering, or continuous integration and continuous delivery (CI/CD) consulting services.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Enterprise software development experience, with the ability to translate requirements into clear technical designs and implementation plans.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Progressive DevOps platform experience, including designing and implementing reliable, scalable systems with clear performance and security trade-offs.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Hands-on experience deploying and managing infrastructure in cloud providers and on-premises environments, including using tools such as Terraform and Ansible.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Ability to write clean, maintainable automation/integration code (e.g., Terraform modules, Ansible roles, scripts) and validate changes with appropriate testing and code review.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Experience performing migrations to GitLab, including using Congregate or similar migration tooling.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Working knowledge of data consistency and integrity concepts (e.g., ACID properties) and how they impact migration design and performance trade-offs.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Strong problem-solving, decision-making, organizational, and time management skills, with the ability to manage multiple priorities with minimal supervision.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Comfort working in a remote, asynchronous environment, using documented decisions (e.g., issues, proposals, and runbooks) to keep work unblocked across time zones while collaborating effectively across GitLab team members, partners, and customer stakeholders.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Bachelor&#39;s Degree in Information Technology, Computer Science, or other advanced technical degree, or equivalent experience&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Professional Services Technical Architect is part of GitLab&#39;s Professional Services organization. We partner with customers who are transitioning to GitLab, expanding how they use an existing GitLab installation, or planning complex upgrades to their infrastructure and processes. Our team brings a diverse set of skills across GitLab deployment, maintenance, and day-to-day usage, along with deep technical knowledge of adjacent tools and platforms. Working closely with Engagement Managers, partner consultants, and customer stakeholders, we focus on delivering high-quality outcomes, sharing best practices, and helping customers realize faster time to value from their GitLab investment. We operate in GitLab&#39;s remote, asynchronous environment and rely on clear documentation and transparent communication to collaborate effectively.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role models skills and behavior aligned with GitLab Values and typically reports to the Regional Delivery Manager. As a Professional Services Technical Architect, you will work more independently than an associate consultant, leveraging deep technical expertise to drive customer outcomes.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;description&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;The base salary range for this role’s listed level is currently for residents of the&amp;nbsp;United States only. This range is intended to reflect the role&#39;s base salary rate in locations throughout the US.&amp;nbsp;Grade level and salary ranges are determined through interviews and a review of education, experience, knowledge, skills, abilities of the applicant, equity with other team members, alignment with market data,&amp;nbsp;and geographic location.&amp;nbsp;The base salary range does not include any bonuses, equity, or benefits. See more information on our &lt;a class=&quot;waffle-rich-text-link&quot; href=&quot;https://about.gitlab.com/handbook/total-rewards/benefits/general-and-entity-benefits/&quot; data-sheets-formula-bar-text-link=&quot;https://bit.ly/GLBeneUS&quot; data-sheets-formula-bar-text-style=&quot;font-size:12px;color:#1155cc;font-weight:normal;text-decoration:underline;font-family:&#39;&#39;Arial&#39;&#39;;font-style:normal;text-decoration-skip-ink:none;&quot;&gt;benefits&lt;/a&gt;&lt;span data-sheets-formula-bar-text-style=&quot;font-size:12px;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;text-decoration:none;font-family:&#39;Arial&#39;;font-style:normal;text-decoration-skip-ink:none;&quot;&gt; and &lt;/span&gt;&lt;a class=&quot;waffle-rich-text-link&quot; href=&quot;https://about.gitlab.com/handbook/stock-options/&quot; data-sheets-formula-bar-text-link=&quot;https://bit.ly/GLequity&quot; data-sheets-formula-bar-text-style=&quot;font-size:12px;color:#1155cc;font-weight:normal;text-decoration:underline;font-family:&#39;&#39;Arial&#39;&#39;;font-style:normal;text-decoration-skip-ink:none;&quot;&gt;equity&lt;/a&gt;. Sales roles are also eligible for incentive pay targeted at up to 100% of the offered base salary.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;