&lt;p&gt;Auterion builds a cutting-edge operating system for autonomous robotic systems that empower a diverse range of platforms to perform surveillance, reconnaissance, inspection, mapping and logistics tasks. Our industry-leading software drives the adoption of robotic fleets and is recognized by the U.S. government as the future standard for its drone programs.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for a &lt;strong&gt;Senior Embedded Performance Engineer&lt;/strong&gt; who is passionate about getting the most out of embedded systems — from low-level Linux tuning and hardware integration to high-performance video and data pipelines. This role is ideal for someone who enjoys working close to hardware, moving across the stack, and solving the kinds of problems where milliseconds, bandwidth, startup time, and system efficiency matter.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will work across the AuterionOS ecosystem on topics such as:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Embedded Linux performance and system tuning&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Low-latency video streaming and media pipelines&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;C/C++, Python, and Bash-based platform development&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hardware integration, system profiling, and end-to-end optimization&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaboration with experienced and driven engineers across Auterion&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work within the Apps &amp;amp; Simulation team and collaborate with other development teams to build high-performance products for autonomous systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design, optimize, and maintain performance-critical components within AuterionOS, Auterion’s custom embedded Linux distribution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Improve end-to-end system behavior across compute, networking, video, and hardware interfaces, with a strong focus on latency, throughput, reliability, and resource efficiency.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Analyze and optimize demanding workloads such as real-time telemetry, video streaming, media processing, and communication between distributed system components.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Investigate system bottlenecks across the full stack, from kernel and OS behavior to application-level code and tooling.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with engineering and product teams to understand both internal and customer use cases, and translate them into robust technical solutions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Propose and implement new platform capabilities with a strong emphasis on measurable performance gains in real-world deployments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Participate in daily stand-ups, release planning, and prioritization discussions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Qualifications and Skills&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;B.Sc. or M.Sc. in Computer Science, Software Engineering, or a related field.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of professional experience writing object-oriented C++ and/or Python.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep experience with embedded Linux systems, including cross-compilation, debugging, profiling, and performance tuning.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong hands-on background in diagnosing and optimizing real-world system behavior, including CPU, memory, I/O, networking, boot time, and application latency.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building or optimizing low-latency video or data-streaming pipelines, ideally on embedded platforms.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent understanding of software systems that span embedded devices, higher-level applications, and fully integrated products.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong software engineering fundamentals, including system design, implementation, debugging, and testing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with video codecs, GStreamer, RTP/RTSP, or hardware-accelerated media pipelines.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Solid experience with Debian/Ubuntu-based systems, Bash scripting, and systemd.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with Docker and docker-compose in complex development and deployment environments, as well as qemu.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong debugging and performance analysis skills at both system and application level, combined with a proactive and self-directed working style.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficient in ROS2/DDS-style middleware and experienced with networking across multiple OSI layers, including REST APIs and performance-sensitive communication paths.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with system integration and interfacing sensors or peripherals, especially via USB and Ethernet.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working in an agile engineering environment with stand-ups, sprint planning, and shared ownership across teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bonus: Experience with build systems such as CMake, including improving build performance in large-scale software projects.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Benefits&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Flexible working hours&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Stock Options&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Generous holiday allowance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Company pension plan&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Car parking&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Enhanced maternity &amp;amp; paternity leave&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mental health and wellbeing support&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Learning and development opportunities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Auterion&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are building the leading software platform for AI-powered autonomous systems for enterprise and government customers. Our team is supporting the most important missions and solving the most challenging problems.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Auterion, we bring together the sharpest minds who love to solve the hardest problems. Join a vibrant team built on innovation, openness, and excellence, where you’ll be empowered to develop ideas, collaborate across all levels, and make an impact that matters.&lt;/p&gt;<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.ch/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Switzerland</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;GitLab is the intelligent orchestration platform for DevSecOps. GitLab enables organizations to increase developer productivity, improve operational efficiency, reduce security and compliance risk, and accelerate digital transformation. More than 50 million registered users and more than 50% of the Fortune 100* trust GitLab to ship better, more secure software faster.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The same principles built into our products are reflected in how our team works: we embrace AI as a core productivity multiplier, with all team members expected to incorporate AI into their daily workflows to drive efficiency, innovation, and impact. GitLab is where careers accelerate, innovation flourishes, and every voice is valued. Our high-performance culture is driven by our values&amp;nbsp;and continuous knowledge exchange, enabling our team members to reach their full potential while collaborating with industry leaders to solve complex problems. &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=OuZIb5zszQI&quot;&gt;Co-create the future with us&lt;/a&gt; as we build technology that transforms how the world develops software.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;*&lt;em&gt;Fortune 500® is a registered trademark of Fortune Media IP Limited, used under license. Claim based on GitLab data. Fortune 100 refers to the top 20% ranked companies in the 2025 Fortune 500 list, published in June 2025. Fortune and Fortune Media IP Limited are not affiliated with, and do not endorse products or services of GitLab.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This position is 100% remote and will be based in the United States and Canada.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Pipeline Programs Manager turns GitLab&#39;s pipeline targets into programs the field can run. You&#39;ll own execution of pipeline generation programs, including sales plays, PipeGen days, and run the hygiene checkpoints that keep pipeline data trustworthy. You&#39;ll also help surface the risks and upside behind our pipeline plan working across Sales, Marketing, Field Enablement, Sales Strategy, and RevOps.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You&#39;ll Do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Execute global and regional pipeline generation programs, including codified sales plays and PipeGen days, against an established program calendar.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate in-quarter program delivery across regions and segments: timelines, owners, communications, and follow-through on action items.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Run weekly, monthly, and quarterly pipeline hygiene checkpoints, and report on adherence and trends with RevOps and Sales Strategy.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Marketing and Enablement to bring pipeline generation programs to the field with the right messaging, content, and training.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with the team on the GTM plan by identifying the drivers, risks, and upside that could move the pipeline numbers, and making them visible to decision-makers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Give input on the design of sales plays, hygiene standards, and related incentives from what you see during execution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track program performance against success measures, and summarize what worked, what didn&#39;t, and what to change next time.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate global outbound program execution with Sales Development and sales leaders, and help bring it to regional and team levels at scale.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify process and systems improvements in Salesforce and reporting that increase metric visibility and reduce manual work, and work with RevOps and Systems to land them.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You&#39;ll Bring&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ Years experience in Sales, Sales Programs, Sales Operations, Revenue Operations, Field or Sales Enablement, or Marketing Operations, with a record of delivering programs on time and with quality.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience running cross-functional programs with operational rigor: multiple stakeholders, competing priorities, and clear follow-through.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfort working with pipeline data. You can use Salesforce and BI dashboards to spot gaps and explain what they mean. Basic SQL (Snowflake or similar) is a plus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understanding of the B2B sales funnel: pipeline creation, conversion, velocity, and hygiene.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Clear communication and presentation skills. You can explain a program or a risk to Sales leaders and to cross-functional partners.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to influence without authority, earning trust and moving work forward across teams you don&#39;t manage.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Good judgment in a fast-moving environment. You move quickly, keep quality high, and know when to escalate.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Curiosity about how AI and automation can improve go-to-market execution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ownership mindset. You carry programs through to outcomes, not just activity.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in a quota-carrying or sales role is a plus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Pipeline Excellence team builds the pipeline engine that turns GitLab&#39;s growth targets into predictable, repeatable revenue outcomes. We set pipeline targets and the GTM plan, run the programs and cadence that keep the field moving, and turn pipeline data into recommendations on where to invest.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We work with Speed with Quality, so our cadence and standards let go-to-market teams move fast without sacrificing forecast accuracy. We hold an Ownership Mindset, meaning every stage of the funnel has a defined owner and standard. We measure ourselves on Customer Outcomes: pipeline health exists to drive real bookings and real customer relationships, not just activity. We work closely with Sales leadership, Sales Strategy, Marketing, Field Enablement, Sales Development, Finance, and Analytics, and we&#39;re scaling that engine for the agentic era.&lt;/p&gt;
